  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Second wave – 1 v 1 that becomes 2 v 1",
  "description": "Half court, one goal with a goalkeeper. Three lines at the centre line: line A by the left boards with balls, line B in the middle and line C by the right boards, also with balls. A passes to B and sprints towards goal. B plays the ball straight back into A's run and becomes the defender. A takes B on 1 v 1 and tries to get a shot away.\n\nWhen the 1 v 1 is over – a shot or B wins the ball – C sets off with a new ball. A and C now attack 2 v 1 against B, with at most two passes before the shot. Rotation: A to line B, B to line C and C to line A. Run it as much from the other side.\n\nVariants: allow only one pass in the 2 v 1. Or run just the 1 v 1 part as a defending drill with two lines, then let the defender start from the centre line by the far boards so they have further to go to get in front of the attacker. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attacker: receive at full speed and go straight at goal in the 1 v 1."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Defender: close the gap right after the pass and steer the attacker out towards the boards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "2 v 1: commit the defender with the ball before you pass, and keep your distance from your teammate."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Decide quickly – shoot yourself if the defender covers the pass."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
